  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-10-28T03:52:51.858Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is due to use of `enumValueIndex` in `VRCSDK\\Dependencies\\VRChat\\Editor\\Components3\\VRCAvatarDescriptorEditor3AnimLayerGui.cs`\nThe net result of this is, the layers are off by 1 between Inspector and Debug. And if you reset to default, your layers will be offset:\n![Debug and Normal inspectors show layers in different order](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/733160520173223946/770854461912514600/inspector_mismatch.png)\nThe immediate cause is the `VRCAvatarDescriptor.AnimLayerType` enum value for `SpecialIK `was removed. The order remained the same, and the values remained the same, but anything uses the \"enum index\" will break, including the VRCSDK3 VRCAvatarDescriptor Inspector.",
